   "text": {
    "L1": "A grid map uses columns and rows to name each square.",
    "L2": "The column comes first and the row comes second, so this square is C2.",
    "L3": "To follow a path, count moves from the square where you start. Do not count the starting square.",
    "L4": "From A1 to C4, move two steps right, then three steps up.",
    "L5": "The path ends at C4, where the swing is located.",
    "L6": "Here is a myth: changing the order of the moves makes no difference.",
    "L7": "That is not true. Two right then three up reaches C4, but three right then two up reaches D3.",
    "L8": "Now use the same rule: start at A1, move three steps right and two steps up. Tap the ending square."
   },
